  <data name="TourWelcomeTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Welcome to the JiggleForge beta</value></data>
  <data name="TourWelcomeDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>This tour introduces every page and key control. JiggleForge modifies the selected Mod folder, so keep a backup before testing an important Mod.</value></data>
  <data name="TourOpenProjectTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Open a Mod project</value></data>
  <data name="TourOpenProjectDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Drop one character Mod folder here, or select Choose folder. Do not select the entire Mods or _MANAGED_ directory.</value></data>
  <data name="TourZzmiTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Select the ZZMI root</value></data>
  <data name="TourZzmiDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Select the ZZMI root containing Mods and ShaderFixes. It is usually under %APPDATA%\XXMI Launcher\ZZMI.</value></data>
  <data name="TourRuntimeTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Install or update the runtime</value></data>
  <data name="TourRuntimeDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use this after first launch, an app update, or a game update. Return to the game and press F10 when installation finishes.</value></data>
  <data name="TourDragKeysTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Set global drag keys</value></data>
  <data name="TourDragKeysDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>You may select multiple mouse or keyboard buttons. Original characters and adapted Mods share these global drag keys.</value></data>
  <data name="TourWheelTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enable wheel depth input</value></data>
  <data name="TourWheelDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Start WheelBridge to control depth with the mouse wheel. It is not required for screen-plane dragging only.</value></data>
  <data name="TourDrawsTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Identify, name, and group Draws</value></data>
  <data name="TourDrawsDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each Draw represents one adapted draw call from the source Mod. Rename it, disable deformation, or place related Draws in the same group. This page is empty until a project is open.</value></data>
  <data name="TourInspectorTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>In-game Draw inspector</value></data>
  <data name="TourInspectorDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Enable it while identifying model parts. Press F10 in game, then drag a target to show the matched Draw in the top-left corner. Disable it after configuration.</value></data>
  <data name="TourGraphModeTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose a dependency editor</value></data>
  <data name="TourGraphModeDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use the edge list or switch to the interactive graph, where nodes can be moved and connected with the right mouse button.</value></data>
  <data name="TourEdgesTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Set influence between groups</value></data>
  <data name="TourEdgesDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>A directed edge means dragging the source group also moves the destination group. Dependencies are transitive; avoid unwanted cycles and cross-part influence.</value></data>
  <data name="TourMaskTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Assign texture Masks to Draws</value></data>
  <data name="TourMaskDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>White has a weight near 1 and black near 0. Without a Mask, the entire Draw deforms with a default weight of 1.0.</value></data>
  <data name="TourPhysicsScopeTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Select a physics scope</value></data>
  <data name="TourPhysicsScopeDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Edit the project defaults or assign independent settings to each Draw group.</value></data>
  <data name="TourPhysicsTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Tune deformation feel</value></data>
  <data name="TourPhysicsDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Radius and strength define reach and magnitude. Frequency, damping, maximum offset, depth range, and volume response define the feel.</value></data>
  <data name="TourReplayTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Replay this tour at any time</value></data>
  <data name="TourReplayDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>When finished, apply the configuration at the bottom of the page and press F10 in game. Replay the complete tour from here later.</value></data>
  <data name="TourCommunityTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Join the QQ community</value></data>
  <data name="TourCommunityDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>QQ group: 451901293. Join us for questions, suggestions, update news, or simply to chat.</value></data>
