  <data name="UninstallApplicationButton.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Prepare removal…</value></data>
  <data name="ApplicationUninstallDialogTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose how to uninstall</value></data>
  <data name="ApplicationUninstallDialogIntro" xml:space="preserve"><value>Both options stop WheelBridge and remove the global deformation runtime. To avoid security-software false positives, JiggleForge does not delete itself. When preparation is complete, the application folder opens so you can delete it manually. Choose how adapted Mods should be handled.</value></data>
  <data name="ApplicationUninstallKeepTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Keep compatibility layer</value></data>
  <data name="ApplicationUninstallKeepDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Keep each Mod's JiggleForge configuration and original backup, and install a lightweight compatibility layer that performs no drawing or computation. Mods render normally without deformation; reinstalling the JiggleForge runtime later makes them usable again.</value></data>
  <data name="ApplicationUninstallFullTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Restore Mods and prepare removal</value></data>
  <data name="ApplicationUninstallFullDescription" xml:space="preserve"><value>Validate every JiggleForge.original.zip and restore adapted Mods recorded by the app or found in the current ZZMI. If an existing Mod has no valid backup, uninstall stops and shows its exact path.</value></data>
